FILE: app/src/fly-controls.ts
```ts
import type { FreeCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import { attachConfigurableFreeControl } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function attachFlyControls(
  camera: FreeCamera,
  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,
  scene: SceneContext,
): () => void {
  return attachConfigurableFreeControl(camera, canvas, scene, {
    upKeys: ["Space"],
    downKeys: ["PageDown"],
    fastKeys: ["ShiftLeft", "ShiftRight"],
    fastMultiplier: 3,
  });
}
```

I used the library’s configurable free-camera control with Space as the only up key, PageDown as the only down key, and both Shift keys as the 3× fast key, then returned its dispose function so no extra listeners or frame work remain. I was not sure whether `attachConfigurableFreeControl` is exported from the `@babylonjs/lite` root in the real package, since only the camera declarations were available here.
